WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:06.180
Welcome to our second drink of Goodbye, Toby, part one.
欢迎来到我们对《再见，托比》上集的第二杯饮品播客。

2
00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:09.960
This episode kicks off the end of season four of The Office.
这一集拉开了《办公室》第四季大结局的序幕。

3
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:10.600
Wow.
哇。

4
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:11.200
Yeah.
是啊。

5
00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:16.920
We had a lot of fun folks from our office family sharing behind-the-scenes details with us for this two-parter.
我们有很多办公室大家庭的有趣成员，和我们分享了这两集幕后的细节。

6
00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:22.320
So thank you once again to Jen Salata, Paul Lieberstein, Kit Zabornak, and Creed Bratton.
所以再次感谢詹·萨拉塔、保罗·李伯斯坦、基特·扎博纳克以及克里德·布拉顿。

7
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.820
Angela, this is also the episode where we got into a debate about what the phrase hot to trot means.
安吉拉，这也是我们卷入一场关于“hot to trot”这个短语是什么意思的辩论的一集。

8
00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:28.880
Yes, I know.
是的，我知道。

9
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.440
People wrote in.
大家来信了。

10
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:31.640
Maria F.
玛丽亚·F

11
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:34.740
said, I first heard hot to trot on Happy Days.
说，我第一次听到“hot to trot”是在《欢乐时光》里。

12
00:00:35.020 --> 00:00:38.040
Richie was going to a dinner at a divorcee's house.
里奇要去一个离异女人的家里吃晚餐。

13
00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:41.720
His friends say, you know what they say about divorcees?
他的朋友说，你知道他们怎么评价离异女人吗？

14
00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:43.200
They're hot to trot.
她们可急不可耐了。

15
00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.140
Jenna is correct.
珍娜是对的。

16
00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.340
Because I said hot to trot means you're—
因为我说“hot to trot”的意思是你——

17
00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.160
Hooking up.
打得火热。

18
00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.340
Yeah, and you said it means you're mad.
对，而你说它的意思是你在生气。

19
00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.400
Yeah, you're coming in hot to trot.
对，你气冲冲地来了。

20
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:54.960
You're ticked off about something.
你为什么事情生气了。

21
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.380
Well, Raquel G.
好吧，拉奎尔·G

22
00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.740
says, Angela, I have also used hot to trot in the same way you did.
说，安吉拉，我也用过和你一样意思的“hot to trot”。

23
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:02.160
And Linda G.
然后琳达·G

24
00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.680
wants us to know that it has two meanings, and we are both correct.
想让我们知道它有两个意思，我们俩都对。

25
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.220
Thank you, Linda.
谢谢你，琳达。

26
00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:13.560
I do remember a few people DMing me saying, I think you meant like hot under the collar, Angela.
我确实记得有几个人给我发私信说，安吉拉，我想你指的是“气急败坏”吧。

27
00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:15.180
Yes, hot under the collar.
对，气急败坏。

28
00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:16.340
I'm hot under the collar.
我气急败坏了。

29
00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:18.660
This definitely means you're getting mad.
这绝对意味着你在生气。

30
00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:24.580
Well, I still say hot to trot when I'm mad, but I'm more careful where I say it.
好吧，我生气时还是会说“hot to trot”，但我使用它的地方会更小心。

31
00:01:24.780 --> 00:01:26.900
Well, here's a question I have for you.
好吧，我有个问题想问你。

32
00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:34.740
Now that you've learned the second meaning for it, have you ever said to Josh, sweetie, I am hot to trot?
既然你已经知道了它的第二个意思，你有没有对乔什说过，亲爱的，我心痒难耐？

33
00:01:34.900 --> 00:01:34.980
No.
没有。

34
00:01:34.980 --> 00:01:38.180
And he thinks you're mad, but really you mean it the other way?
而他以为你生气了，但实际上你是那个意思？

35
00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:39.780
No, I've never said it.
没有，我从来没说过。

36
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.880
I've never said it.
我从没说过。

37
00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:47.780
Because he probably had to learn in your relationship, if you said, I am hot to trot, it's not what you think.
因为他在你们的恋爱关系中可能不得不学到，如果你说，我心痒难耐，那不是你想的那样。

38
00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:48.780
It's not what you think.
那不是你想的那样。

39
00:01:48.980 --> 00:01:50.900
No, it means you're mad about something.
不，这意味着你在为什么事情生气。

40
00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:51.940
Hmm.
嗯。

41
00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:54.040
I like to keep it interesting.
我喜欢保持新鲜感。

42
00:01:54.360 --> 00:01:56.920
You never know how I'm going to interpret something.
你永远不知道我将如何解读某件事。

43
00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:59.640
Okay, we also got a great background catch.
好吧，我们还得到了一个精彩的背景发现。

44
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:00.680
Louisa C.
路易莎·C

45
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:06.640
said, ladies, at exactly two minutes, I noticed something shiny on Steve's hand.
说，女士们，在正好两分钟的时候，我注意到史蒂夫的手上有个亮晶晶的东西。

46
00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:10.140
I stopped and I saw that Steve had his wedding ring on.
我停下来一看，发现史蒂夫戴着婚戒。

47
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:13.500
All right, Louisa, I went and I looked.
好吧，路易莎，我去了，我也看了。

48
00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.880
You are absolutely right.
你绝对是对的。

49
00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:18.520
It's in the cold open when Michael is dancing through the office.
就在迈克尔在办公室里跳舞的片头冷戏里。

50
00:02:18.520 --> 00:02:19.640
It's part of a montage.
这是蒙太奇镜头的一部分。

51
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:20.800
It's Toby's last day.
今天是托比的最后一天。

52
00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.400
Michael is very excited.
迈克尔非常兴奋。

53
00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.340
And he's sort of doing this scissor move with his arms, like as he's dancing through the office.
而且他一边在办公室里跳舞，一边用手臂做出这种剪刀状的动作。

54
00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:32.620
And when he sort of like slides his arm across the screen, you see his wedding ring.
当他的手臂滑过屏幕时，你能看到他的结婚戒指。

55
00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:36.560
He must have forgotten to take it off, but clearly someone caught it.
他肯定是忘了把它摘下来，但显然有人发现了。

56
00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:41.360
Because then immediately right after, he has a talking head to camera and it's gone.
因为紧接着，他对镜头做了一段访谈，戒指不见了。

57
00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.940
Wow, that's a good catch.
哇，真是个敏锐的发现。

58
00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:50.020
Do you remember that week that Steve jammed his finger playing hockey and he couldn't get his wedding ring off,
你还记得史蒂夫打曲棍球时手指卡住了、摘不下结婚戒指的那周吗？

59
00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.700
so we had to cover it with a Band-Aid?
所以我们不得不拿创可贴把它包起来？

60
00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:52.400
Yes.
是的。

61
00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.180
Oh my gosh, I forgot about that.
噢天哪，我都忘了这事了。

62
00:02:54.180 --> 00:02:57.840
Yeah, because he was like, you're not cutting this off my finger, obviously.
对，因为他当时说，显然你不能把这根手指切了。

63
00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:01.840
So there's, I can't remember what episode it is, but I think it's in season three.
所以，我不记得那是哪一集了，但我想是在第三季。

64
00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.180
We talked about it on the pod.
我们在播客里聊过这件事。

65
00:03:03.920 --> 00:03:06.780
We also got this observation from James L.
我们还收到了来自亚利桑那州的詹姆斯·L.

66
00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:08.340
in Arizona who said,
的观察，他说，

67
00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:11.380
Hi ladies, this is my second listen to the podcaSt.
各位女士好，这是我第二次听这个播客。

68
00:03:11.380 --> 00:03:15.720
I have a long commute and decided to go all the way back to the beginning and listen through again.
我每天上下班通勤时间很长，所以决定从头开始再听一遍。

69
00:03:15.720 --> 00:03:20.800
And I wanted to point out that Pam is wearing a pink sweater in this episode.
我想指出的是，潘在这集里穿了一件粉色毛衣。

70
00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:27.740
It's not the same one that you discuss in a later episode as in Pam's sex sweater theory,
这跟你们在以后某一集里讨论的、也就是潘的“性感毛衣”理论里的不是同一件，

71
00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.420
but I want to throw this out there.
但我还是想提出来交流一下。

72
00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:33.160
Maybe Pam just wears pink when she's feeling extra happy.
也许潘只是在心情格外好的时候才穿粉色。

73
00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:35.760
Loving the second drinks, James.
喜欢第二杯饮品，詹姆斯。

74
00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:37.660
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

75
00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:39.340
She is wearing pink.
她确实穿着粉色。

76
00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:42.200
Yeah, I mean, it's not her sex sweater.
对，我是说，这不是她的性感毛衣。

77
00:03:42.380 --> 00:03:44.300
No, but she does get good news.
对，但她确实得到了好消息。

78
00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.560
She learns about the Pratt Institute,
她得知了普瑞特艺术学院的消息，

79
00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:49.440
and then she's super flirty and gives Jim a little kiss.
然后她超级调情，给了吉姆一个轻轻的吻。

80
00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:50.200
She's happy.
她很高兴。

81
00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:50.680
Yeah.
是啊。

82
00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.640
Well, I love that question.
嗯，我喜欢那个问题。

83
00:03:53.100 --> 00:03:55.460
Well, when we first broke down this episode,
在我们最初剖析这一集的时候，

84
00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:59.080
I shared that there were some awesome Phyllis deleted scenes.
我分享说有一些非常棒的菲莉丝删减片段。

85
00:03:59.640 --> 00:04:03.500
One of my favorites that we discussed was put back in the super fan version.
我们讨论过的一个我最喜欢的片段被加回了超级粉丝版里。

86
00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.160
I really want us to hear it.
我真的很想让我们听听看。

87
00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.500
Okay, to set the scene for you guys,
好的，先给大家交代一下背景，

88
00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:10.260
Phyllis is super stressed about planning the party,
菲莉丝为筹备派对感到压力山大，

89
00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.020
and Jim walks in.
然后吉姆走了进来。

90
00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:13.260
This is so great.
这太棒了。

91
00:04:13.260 --> 00:04:14.460
I'm so glad it's back in.
我太高兴它被加回来了。

92
00:04:14.560 --> 00:04:15.080
You've got to hear it.
你们一定要听听。

93
00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:17.840
Well, who can do a party of this size?
嗯，谁能办得起这么大规模的派对呢？

94
00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:19.840
But you're in the business.
但你是做这一行的。

95
00:04:20.180 --> 00:04:22.260
You must surely know of some other businesses.
你肯定知道其他一些同行吧。

96
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:24.840
Okay, well, I just want a damn dance floor.
好吧，我只是想要一个该死的舞池。

97
00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:25.760
I'm sorry.
我很抱歉。

98
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:26.740
So sorry.
非常抱歉。

99
00:04:26.820 --> 00:04:27.460
I shouldn't have sworn.
我不该说脏话的。

100
00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:28.200
I'm so sorry.
真的很抱歉。

101
00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.240
Thanks for your time.
谢谢你抽出时间。

102
00:04:31.420 --> 00:04:31.860
What?
什么？

103
00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:33.920
Sorry.
对不起。

104
00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.300
I shouldn't have said what like that.
我不该那样说话的。

105
00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:36.860
It was really rude.
真的很粗鲁。

106
00:04:37.180 --> 00:04:37.720
Scared me.
吓死我了。

107
00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:39.920
How's the party planning going?
派对筹备得怎么样了？

108
00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.560
Jim, I am so f***ed.
吉姆，我死定了。

109
00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:43.360
So it's going great, it sounds like.
听起来进展得很顺利嘛。

110
00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:44.100
I don't know.
我不知道。

111
00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:45.120
I'm not used to the stress.
我不习惯这种压力。

112
00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:51.350
I should say, the top of the scene, she's pacing on the phone.
我得说，在这一幕开头，她在边走边打电话。

113
00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.650
She's with some type of like event, you know, party rental place.
她正和某种活动、你知道的，派对租赁公司联系。

114
00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:55.090
Yes.
是的。

115
00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.210
Oh my gosh.
哦天哪。

116
00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:57.010
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

117
00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:58.210
Well, that was all amazing.
嗯，那些都太棒了。

118
00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.870
Everyone, now here is your second drink of Goodbye, Toby, part one.
各位，这是你们的第二杯《再见，托比》第一集特饮。

119
00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:07.150
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍。

120
00:05:07.330 --> 00:05:08.450
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金西。

121
00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:09.730
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演过《办公室》。

122
00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:10.970
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

123
00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:14.810
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们专为你带来《办公室》终极重温播客。

124
00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:19.010
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind the
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并带来独家幕后

125
00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:21.790
scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
故事，只有身处其中的我们两个才能告诉你。

126
00:05:21.970 --> 00:05:22.930
We're The Office ladies.
我们是办公室女士。

127
00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.060
Hello, everyone.
大家好。

128
00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:29.280
Howdy.
哈喽。

129
00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.900
Today, we are breaking down Goodbye, Toby, part one.
今天，我们要剖析《再见，托比》第一集。

130
00:05:34.420 --> 00:05:35.620
I can't believe it.
真不敢相信。

131
00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:36.800
We're at the end of season four.
我们已经到第四季末了。

132
00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:38.600
I can't believe it, Jenna.
真不敢相信，珍娜。

133
00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:39.980
I'm excited, though.
不过我很兴奋。

134
00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:41.220
This is such a good episode.
这真是一集好剧。

135
00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:42.540
Oh, I loved it.
哦，我太喜欢了。

136
00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.040
Beyond loved it.
岂止是喜欢。

137
00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:52.320
It is season four, episode 18, written by Jen Salata and Paul Lieberstein and directed by
这是第四季第18集，由珍·萨拉塔和保罗·利伯斯坦编剧，导演是

138
00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:53.240
Paul Feig.
保罗·费格。

139
00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.540
Hashtag beyond loved.
话题标签：岂止是喜欢。

140
00:05:56.200 --> 00:05:58.160
Yeah, beyond loved.
对，岂止是喜欢。

141
00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:02.040
Well, I know you've got a great summary and some fast facts.
好了，我知道你准备了精彩的摘要和一些快讯。

142
00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:03.160
I can't wait to hear them.
我等不及想听了。

143
00:06:03.420 --> 00:06:04.240
Let's get started.
我们开始吧。

144
00:06:04.720 --> 00:06:07.080
Toby is moving to Costa Rica.
托比要搬去哥斯达黎加了。

145
00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.440
Finally, his lifelong dream is coming true.
终于，他一生的梦想成真了。

146
00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:15.840
Michael insists the party planning committee plan a huge going away party.
迈克尔坚决要求派对筹备委员会举办一场盛大的欢送派对。

147
00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:19.700
And when Angela balks, he puts Phyllis in charge.
当安吉拉退缩时，他让菲利斯来负责。

148
00:06:20.180 --> 00:06:22.700
Oh, can you believe it?
哦，你敢相信吗？

149
00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:25.080
I mean, she does a really good job.
我是说，她干得真的很棒。

150
00:06:25.300 --> 00:06:25.980
You know what?
你知道吗？

151
00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:27.000
I don't need to hear it.
我不想听这个。

152
00:06:27.200 --> 00:06:29.140
Well, I'm going to talk about it more later.
好吧，我等下还要多谈谈这个。

153
00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:30.120
Well, OK.
好吧，行。

154
00:06:30.120 --> 00:06:34.980
There is a new HR representative coming in, Holly Flax.
有个新的人力资源代表要来，霍莉·弗拉克斯。

155
00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:39.240
She will be taking over for Toby, and this is her first day at Dunder Mifflin.
她将接替托比，这是她来到邓德米弗林的头一天。

156
00:06:39.620 --> 00:06:43.580
Michael assumes he will hate her, but he is quickly smitten.
迈克尔本以为自己会讨厌她，但他很快就迷上了她。

157
00:06:44.060 --> 00:06:45.100
Very quickly.
非常快。

158
00:06:45.480 --> 00:06:46.340
Very quickly.
非常快。

159
00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:47.600
But that is Michael.
但这就是迈克尔。

160
00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:49.640
I mean, Michael falls in love at Hello.
我的意思是，迈克尔一听见“你好”就坠入爱河了。

161
00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:50.780
He does.
确实如此。

162
00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:55.540
Meanwhile, Pam gets some good news.
与此同时，帕姆听到了一些好消息。

163
00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:56.820
Should we get started?
我们开始吧？

164
00:06:58.040 --> 00:06:59.140
Fast fact number one.
快讯第一条。

165
00:06:59.360 --> 00:07:02.540
I thought you were going to like tip your hand a little bit.
我还以为你会稍微透漏一点底牌呢。

166
00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.300
Is it tip your hand or tip your hat?
是叫“透漏底牌”还是“脱帽致敬”？

167
00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:05.260
It's tip your hat.
是“脱帽致敬”。

168
00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:10.020
No, I think it's your hand because you're playing poker and you tip it and people see your cards.
不对，我觉得是“透漏底牌”，因为你玩扑克时把牌歪一下，别人就看到你的牌了。

169
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:10.820
Right.
没错。

170
00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.000
But you tip your hat for something else.
但你脱帽是为了别的事。

171
00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:13.560
A hello?
打招呼吗？

172
00:07:13.860 --> 00:07:14.300
Maybe.
也许吧。

173
00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:18.320
But I thought you were going to hint at what Pam's big news was.
不过我以为你会暗示帕姆的大好消息是什么。

174
00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.840
But no, let's get into some fast facts.
但好吧，我们先来聊点快讯。

175
00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:21.560
All right.
好吧。

176
00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:22.920
Let's not tip anything.
我们什么都不透漏。

177
00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:24.800
We're tipping nothing right now.
我们现在什么都不透漏。

178
00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:25.460
Tip nothing.
什么都不透漏。

179
00:07:26.100 --> 00:07:27.420
Fast fact number one.
快讯第一条。

180
00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:31.220
I find it very funny that Paul had to write himself out of the show.
我觉得保罗不得不把自己的角色写出剧本，这非常有趣。

181
00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:33.260
I thought it was funny, too.
我也觉得挺有趣的。

182
00:07:33.480 --> 00:07:37.260
But knowing Paul, because he's very practical, it was probably like, well, it needs to be done.
但了解保罗的性格，因为他很务实，他可能觉得，好吧，这事必须得做。

183
00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:41.900
There is a very practical reason for why he wrote himself out of the show that we know.
他把自己写出剧本背后，有一个我们都知道的很实际的原因。

184
00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:48.260
Paul and Jen are going to take over as the showrunners of The Office starting in season five
从第五季开始，保罗和珍将接任《办公室》的剧集运作人，

185
00:07:48.260 --> 00:07:51.940
because Greg was going to be working on Parks and Recreation.
因为格雷格要去负责《公园与游憩》。没错。

186
00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:52.640
Yep.
没错。

187
00:07:53.000 --> 00:07:54.300
Now, Greg was still around.
现在，格雷格还在。

188
00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:56.040
He had a foot in both worlds.
他两边都兼顾着。

189
00:07:56.340 --> 00:07:58.860
Yeah, he'd pop by, but he wasn't going to be there day to day.
对，他会过来看看，但不会每天都在那儿。

190
00:07:59.380 --> 00:08:00.780
That was Jen and Paul.
那是珍和保罗负责。

191
00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:06.500
So they teamed up to write this episode and they were really trying to set themselves up for next season.
所以他们合作写了这一集，并且他们真的是在为下一季做准备。

192
00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:08.240
Paul needed a break from the acting.
保罗需要从演戏中抽身休息一下。

193
00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:10.640
He wanted to concentrate on writing the show.
他想专注于剧本创作。

194
00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:14.820
So we traded emails with Paul and he sent in an audio clip all about it.
所以我们和保罗通过邮件交流，他还发来了一段关于这事的音频片段。

195
00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:19.220
Jen Salata and I were taking over as showrunners for season five,
珍·萨拉塔和我将接任第五季的剧集运作人，

196
00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:22.020
and that was absolutely part of getting rid of me.
这绝对是把我弄走的一部分原因。

197
00:08:22.420 --> 00:08:25.320
Give me some time to just showrun and concentrate on that.
给我一些时间来专门负责剧集运作并集中精力。

198
00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:28.080
Did we know for a fact I'd be coming back?
我们当时确切知道我会回来吗？

199
00:08:28.760 --> 00:08:30.480
No, not for a fact.
不，并不确定。

200
00:08:30.660 --> 00:08:33.860
Didn't really think about it that far in.
当时没想那么远。

201
00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.600
There was a lot of things started.
有很多事情拉开了序幕。

202
00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:37.640
Pam's acceptance to art school.
比如潘被艺术学校录取。

203
00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:40.880
Well, that was something we had talked about for a long time.
嗯，那是我们讨论了很久的事情。

204
00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:48.820
We always knew she liked it, but we were looking for, you know, a whole new complication after doing so much with the romance.
我们一直知道她喜欢艺术，但在大搞浪漫之后，你知道的，我们一直在寻找全新的冲突。

205
00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:52.160
And then Angela's engagement to Andy.
还有安吉拉和安迪订婚。

206
00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:56.040
We always knew that was not a relationship to be.
我们一直都知道那不是一段会有结果的感情。

207
00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:59.140
That was a bad relationship, a comedy relationship.
那是一段糟糕的感情，一段充满喜剧色彩的感情。

208
00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:02.060
But it gave us some fun stuff, obviously.
但显然，它给我们带来了一些有趣的内容。

209
00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:07.000
There's so many big storylines that they set up with this finale.
他们在这集季终集里铺垫了那么多重大的故事情节。

210
00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:08.240
I know.
我知道。

211
00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.740
I mean, we haven't even talked about Jan.
我是说，我们甚至还没聊到简。

212
00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:11.860
That's part two.
那是第二部分。

213
00:09:12.060 --> 00:09:12.980
But my goodness.
我的天哪。

214
00:09:13.360 --> 00:09:13.980
Oh, I know.
哦，我懂。

215
00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.040
Big, big.
太重大了。

216
00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:16.000
What do they call it?
他们管这叫什么来着？

217
00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.360
The cliffhanger.
悬念。

218
00:09:18.240 --> 00:09:19.280
Big cliffhanger.
巨大的悬念。

219
00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:22.880
Why am I having a hard time with like common phrases today?
为什么我今天连常用短语都说不好？

220
00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:26.540
Buckle in, everybody, because this might be a bumpy ride.
大家都系好安全带，因为这可能会是一段颠簸的旅程。

221
00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:27.840
Well, I'm here for it.
好吧，我奉陪到底。

222
00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:30.280
I love when you mangle common phrases.
我就喜欢你把常用短语说得乱七八糟的。

223
00:09:30.540 --> 00:09:32.140
It's one of my favorite things about you.
这是我最喜欢你的地方之一。

224
00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:33.160
I don't know why.
我也不知道为什么。

225
00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.360
I almost said it's like the cliff's edge.
我刚才差点说成是悬崖边。

226
00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.360
And then in my brain, I was like, no, no, no.
然后我在脑子里想，不，不，不。

227
00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:38.940
That's not right.
那不对。

228
00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:39.900
You'll find it, lady.
你会想起来的，女士。

229
00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:41.840
All right.
好吧。

230
00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:42.360
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

231
00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:43.660
Fast fact number two.
趣味冷知识之二。

232
00:09:44.120 --> 00:09:44.240
Yeah.
对。

233
00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:48.860
Jen Salata said that this script took about five days to write.
珍·萨拉塔说这个剧本大概花了五天时间来写。

234
00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:49.960
Five days.
五天。

235
00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:51.100
That's crazy.
太疯狂了。

236
00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:53.140
How did they do it in five days?
他们怎么能在五天内写完的？

237
00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.820
It would take me so long to write this.
我要是来写这个得花好久好久。

238
00:09:54.980 --> 00:09:56.220
This is a juggernaut.
这简直是个庞然大物。

239
00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:56.940
I know.
我知道。

240
00:09:57.160 --> 00:10:02.220
She said they had an outline and they divided up the work and they each wrote different parts
她说他们先列了个大纲，然后分工合作，各自负责写不同的部分

241
00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:05.420
and then they put it all together and they did a rewrite together.
然后把它们拼到一起，又一起进行了一次重写。

242
00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.440
So, I mean, I guess there were two people on it, but still.
所以，我的意思是，我猜是有两个人负责，但还是很厉害。

243
00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:17.760
Also, the original cut of this episode came in at 72 minutes and they had to cut it down to 40 minutes.
另外，这集的最初剪辑版长达72分钟，而他们不得不把它剪短到40分钟。

244
00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:18.560
Lady.
天呐。

245
00:10:18.860 --> 00:10:22.220
Guess who found her shooting draft of Goodbye, Toby?
猜猜谁找到了《再见，托比》的拍摄初稿？

246
00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.500
You, electronic hoarder.
你，电子产品囤积狂。

247
00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:27.640
Yes, digital hoarder, Angela Kinsey.
没错，数码囤积狂安吉拉·金西。

248
00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:34.500
All right, Jenna, since I have the shooting draft of Goodbye, Toby, I have a little quiz for you.
好吧，珍娜，既然我有《再见，托比》的拍摄初稿，我要对你进行一个小测试。

249
00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:36.860
Oh, all right.
哦，好吧。

250
00:10:37.120 --> 00:10:39.000
You're like, I didn't know I was going to get tested today.
你现在的心情大概是：我可不知道今天要考试啊。

251
00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:39.660
Okay.
好的。

252
00:10:40.000 --> 00:10:44.700
Can you guess how many pages were in the shooting draft?
你猜拍摄剧本有多少页？

253
00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:47.400
Oh, well, let me think.
哦，好吧，让我想想。

254
00:10:47.600 --> 00:10:53.480
If I remember correctly, our standard shooting drafts were usually around 30 pages.
如果我没记错的话，我们标准的拍摄剧本通常在 30 页左右。

255
00:10:54.280 --> 00:10:54.520
Yep.
没错。

256
00:10:54.520 --> 00:10:58.900
So, since this was a double episode, I'm going to say 60 pages?
所以，既然这是一集双倍时长的剧集，我猜是 60 页？

257
00:10:59.740 --> 00:11:00.280
75!
75 页！

258
00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:02.880
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

259
00:11:03.180 --> 00:11:06.640
Well, no wonder the original cut came in at 72 minutes.
难怪最初的剪辑版时长达到了 72 分钟。

260
00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:07.620
I know!
就是说啊！

261
00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:12.220
They always say each page of a script equals one minute of screen time.
他们总说剧本每一页相当于一分钟的银幕时间。

262
00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:13.680
On average, right?
平均来说，对吧？

263
00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:18.180
Well, lady, there was so much on the page that did not make it in this episode.
天呐，老兄，剧本里有很多内容最后都没能出现在这一集里。

264
00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:21.140
Well, I'm guessing there are a lot of deleted scenes.
我猜有很多被删减的镜头吧。

265
00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.380
Oh, there's some wonderful deleted scenes.
哦，有一些非常棒的删减镜头。

266
00:11:24.520 --> 00:11:28.060
And then there's even more scenes that aren't in the deleted scenes.
然后还有更多甚至没有被收录进删减镜头的场景。

267
00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:29.500
I really enjoyed this.
我真的很喜欢这个。

268
00:11:29.640 --> 00:11:31.120
I'm going to sprinkle things throughout.
我会在各处穿插一些内容。

269
00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:34.080
And you know what it really made me respect, Jenna?
你知道这让我真正尊敬的是什么吗，珍娜？

270
00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:34.840
What?
什么？

271
00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:35.880
Our editors.
我们的剪辑师。

272
00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.180
I'll tell you why.
我来告诉你为什么。

273
00:11:37.180 --> 00:11:40.200
I re-watched this episode four times.
这部剧我刷了四遍。

274
00:11:40.580 --> 00:11:44.620
And one of the times I re-watched it, I just followed along in the script.
其中有一次我看的时候，手里一直对照着剧本。

275
00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:48.320
And the scenes were moved all around in editing.
在剪辑过程中，场景被调来调去。

276
00:11:48.620 --> 00:11:50.380
I was fascinated by it.
这让我感到非常着迷。

277
00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:55.020
And it really just shows you what storytellers our editors are.
这真的向你展示了我们的剪辑师是多么出色的讲故事能手。

278
00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:57.080
You know, I remember that, Angela.
你知道的，我记得那个，安吉拉。

279
00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:04.040
I remember that they would almost, like, rewrite the script again in the editing process.
我记得他们几乎会在剪辑过程中再次改写剧本一样。

280
00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:04.460
Yeah.
是的。

281
00:12:04.720 --> 00:12:05.820
Because they would do that.
因为他们会那样做。

282
00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.720
But they would move scenes around from where they had been placed in the script originally.
但他们会把场景从剧本最初设定的位置调换到其他地方。

283
00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:10.900
I love that.
我太喜欢这个了。

284
00:12:11.180 --> 00:12:13.900
Well, are you ready for Fast Fact number three?
好了，你准备好听第三条快速冷知识了吗？

285
00:12:14.300 --> 00:12:14.660
Yeah.
准备好了。

286
00:12:15.140 --> 00:12:16.580
Fast Fact number three.
第三条快速冷知识。

287
00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.180
Amy Ryan, a.k.a.
艾米·莱恩，又名

288
00:12:19.340 --> 00:12:21.460
Holly Flax, a.k.a.
霍莉·弗拉克斯，又名

289
00:12:21.800 --> 00:12:22.980
Michael's True Love.
迈克尔的真爱。

290
00:12:23.540 --> 00:12:26.420
Aw, I loved Holly Flax.
噢，我太喜欢霍莉·弗拉克斯了。

291
00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:27.380
I loved her.
我超爱她。

292
00:12:27.780 --> 00:12:31.260
We had a fan question from Zianna G.
我们收到了来自齐安娜·G 的粉丝提问。

293
00:12:31.260 --> 00:12:36.720
Was Amy Ryan asked to play Holly, or did she have to go through the audition process?
艾米·莱恩是受邀出演霍莉的，还是她必须经过试镜流程？

294
00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:40.320
Amy did not have to audition for the role of Holly Flax.
艾米出演霍莉·弗拉克斯这个角色并没有经过试镜。

295
00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:41.960
It was offered to her.
剧组直接把这个角色交给了她。

296
00:12:42.180 --> 00:12:43.260
And this is why.
原因如下。

297
00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:48.700
First of all, Amy Ryan had just been nominated for an Academy Award.
首先，艾米·莱恩刚刚获得奥斯卡奖提名。

298
00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:52.220
We had another Academy Award nominee on our show.
我们的剧组又迎来了一位奥斯卡奖提名者。

299
00:12:52.220 --> 00:12:56.320
She'd been nominated for a movie called Gone Baby Gone.
她因一部名为《失踪宝贝》的电影获得提名。

300
00:12:56.620 --> 00:13:04.180
And in addition to that, the writing staff of The Office was slightly obsessed with the TV show The Wire.
除此之外，《办公室》的编剧团队对电视剧《火线》有点着迷。

301
00:13:04.840 --> 00:13:06.660
And Amy had been on The Wire.
而且艾米出演过《火线》。

302
00:13:06.900 --> 00:13:14.080
And whenever we had, like, big guest star roles come up, the writers would try to get cast members from The Wire to do them.
每当有那种重量级的客串角色出现时，编剧们就会设法找《火线》的演员来演。

303
00:13:14.220 --> 00:13:16.900
I mean, spoiler alert, Idris Elba is coming up.
我的意思是，剧透一下，伊德瑞斯·艾尔巴马上要登场了。

304
00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:17.580
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

305
00:13:17.820 --> 00:13:22.600
But there is actually even more to this story, but we will let Paul Lieberstein tell you.
但其实这个故事还有更多内容，不过我们让保罗·利伯斯坦来告诉大家。

306
00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:27.900
Here's an audio clip from Paul where he also talks about their overall plans for the role of Holly.
这里是保罗的一段音频，他在其中还谈到了他们对霍莉这个角色的整体规划。

307
00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:32.280
Amy Ryan, her agents were asking her, well, what do you want to do?
艾米·莱恩，她的经纪人问她，好吧，你想做什么？

308
00:13:32.380 --> 00:13:33.840
And she said, I want to do The Office.
她说，我想演《办公室》。

309
00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:37.540
And at the very same time, we were talking about her.
而在同一时间，我们正在讨论她。

310
00:13:38.360 --> 00:13:41.720
And I don't really know who reached out to who firSt.
我其实不知道是谁先联系谁的。

311
00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:46.580
I worked with Amy like a million years ago on another show.
我和艾米大约一百万年前在另一档节目里合作过。

312
00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:47.760
And we knew each other.
而且我们认识彼此。

313
00:13:48.280 --> 00:13:50.480
And I was all for it.
我当然全力支持。

314
00:13:50.520 --> 00:13:52.300
I loved working with her both times.
这两次和她合作我都非常愉快。

315
00:13:52.860 --> 00:13:56.240
So we didn't know how much of an arc was it going to be with Amy.
所以我们不知道艾米的戏份会有多长。

316
00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:57.180
We didn't really know.
我们其实并不知道。

317
00:13:57.300 --> 00:13:59.600
We didn't have this kind of long-term deal.
我们没有签这种长期合同。

318
00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:02.080
We wanted to kind of test it out and see.
我们只想试水看看。

319
00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.980
Because you never know about chemistry, right?
因为你永远摸不准化学反应，对吧？

320
00:14:05.060 --> 00:14:07.620
You never know if she's going to have chemistry with Steve.
你永远不知道她和史蒂夫会不会擦出火花。

321
00:14:07.960 --> 00:14:09.000
And she sure did.
而她确实擦出来了。

322
00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:15.140
I don't think we knew that this was going to be the, you know, love of his life.
我想我们当时并不知道这将是他的，你知道的，一生挚爱。

323
00:14:15.280 --> 00:14:17.620
We hadn't planned it that far in the head.
我们没有提前规划那么远。

324
00:14:17.800 --> 00:14:20.720
We were also watching what happened and reacting to it.
我们也是在边看事态发展边做出反应。

325
00:14:21.780 --> 00:14:23.760
Can you believe that she said The Office?
你能相信她说过想演《办公室》吗？

326
00:14:24.120 --> 00:14:25.740
I was so tickled by that.
我对此感到高兴极了。

327
00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:30.960
I mean, she did this interview where she said she had been doing these heavy dramas.
我是说，她做过一个采访，说她一直在拍那些沉重的正剧。

328
00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:33.660
And she really wanted to lighten things up.
她真的很想轻松一下。

329
00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:34.980
She wanted to do a comedy.
她想演喜剧。

330
00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.580
And she loved our show.
而且她很喜欢我们的节目。

331
00:14:36.760 --> 00:14:39.360
So that's what she told her agent she wanted to do.
所以这就是她告诉经纪人她想做的事。

332
00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:42.500
Here are her crossover The Office connections.
以下是她与《办公室》的交叉人脉。

333
00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.560
Jenna, she was not on Monk.
珍娜，她没有演过《神探阿蒙》。

334
00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.780
Oh, no, she wasn't on Monk.
哦，不，她没演过《神探阿蒙》。

335
00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:51.740
But the show that her and Paul worked on was in the 90s.
但她和保罗合作的那部剧是在90年代。

336
00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:54.660
And it was called The Naked Truth with Taya Leone.
它叫《赤裸真相》，由蒂娅·里欧妮主演。

337
00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:57.060
And Paul Lieberstein was a writer on it.
保罗·利伯斯坦是该剧的编剧之一。

338
00:14:57.180 --> 00:14:58.120
So that's where they met.
所以他们就是在那儿认识的。

339
00:14:58.340 --> 00:15:04.320
And then she and Steve Carell did a movie together in 2007 called Dan in Real Life.
然后她和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔在2007年合作过一部电影叫《老爸行不行》。

340
00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.900
So they had worked together before.
所以他们以前就合作过。

341
00:15:06.520 --> 00:15:06.800
Yes.
是的。

342
00:15:07.180 --> 00:15:13.020
Kentapedia told me that they had locked her down for six episodes for season five when
肯塔百科告诉我，当她进行这次客串时，

343
00:15:13.020 --> 00:15:14.280
she did this guest role.
他们已经把第五季的六集戏份敲定给她了。

344
00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:15.800
But that's as far as they went.
但也就到此为止了。

345
00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:20.740
And kind of like what Paul said, they didn't know if this was going to be a temporary love
有点像保罗所说的，他们不知道这会不会是迈克尔的一个临时

346
00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:21.660
interest for Michael.
恋爱对象。

347
00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:22.820
They weren't sure.
他们很不确定。

348
00:15:23.060 --> 00:15:27.060
But they did have her set to start off the next season.
但他们确实安排了她回归开启下一季。

349
00:15:27.460 --> 00:15:31.320
There are so many great scenes between Holly and Michael in this episode.
这集里霍莉和迈克尔之间有太多精彩的对手戏了。

350
00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.920
And there are even more wonderful ones in the script.
剧本里还有更多美妙的片段。

351
00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:36.080
I really wish they all could have stayed in.
我真的很希望他们所有人都能留下来。

352
00:15:36.220 --> 00:15:37.380
I know they had to trim them.
我知道他们不得不删减一些片段。

353
00:15:37.500 --> 00:15:43.220
But you really see the build of their sort of mutual, like, crush on each other.
但你真的能看出他们那种互相对彼此有好感的铺垫。

354
00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:45.900
I got choked up watching this episode.
我看这集的时候都哽咽了。

355
00:15:46.060 --> 00:15:52.540
Every time she returns his affection or flirts with him a little bit.
每次她回应他的爱意或者跟他稍微调情一下。

356
00:15:52.600 --> 00:15:58.700
I mean, I was so excited for Michael that a woman was being kind to him.
我是说，我为迈克尔感到太兴奋了，有个女人对他这么好。

357
00:15:58.840 --> 00:16:00.280
I mean, I was emotional.
我是说，我很激动。

358
00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:02.680
Not just kind, but she gets him.
不仅是好，而且她懂他。

359
00:16:02.680 --> 00:16:04.160
They have the same humor.
他们有相同的幽默感。

360
00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:05.140
Yes.
是的。

361
00:16:05.500 --> 00:16:06.880
Well, lady, that's all I got.
好吧，女士，我只有这些了。

362
00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.060
Should we take a break and then we'll come back and get into this episode?
我们要不要休息一下，然后回来聊聊这一集？

363
00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:11.040
Let's do it.
好的。

364
00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.460
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
注意了，所有WDNC的新老会员。

365
00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:21.700
I'm Melanie Sanders.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯。

366
00:16:21.700 --> 00:16:24.340
And this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
这里是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客节目。

367
00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:28.540
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们到了中年，意识到我们真的没那么多心思去在乎了。

368
00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:34.200
Now we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling
现在我们得互相帮助，去搞懂潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、不靠谱的

369
00:16:34.200 --> 00:16:36.640
families, brain fog and bat wings.
家人、脑雾和蝴蝶袖。

370
00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.500
We are not alone and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听见。

371
00:16:39.740 --> 00:16:41.400
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

372
00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:46.200
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get
在你获取播客的任何地方关注并收听由梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的“我们不在乎俱乐部”

373
00:16:46.200 --> 00:16:46.780
your podcaSt.
播客。

374
00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:51.910
All right.
好了。

375
00:16:52.010 --> 00:16:55.230
We are back with a classic gym prank.
我们回来了，这是一个经典的健身房恶作剧。

376
00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:58.910
This is our cold open and Michael is not in it.
这是我们的开场白，迈克尔没在里面。

377
00:16:59.090 --> 00:16:59.610
Did you notice?
你注意到了吗？

378
00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:00.770
I did notice.
我确实注意到了。

379
00:17:01.130 --> 00:17:02.290
His door is shut.
他的门是关着的。

380
00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:05.950
We're being led to believe that Steve is behind that door, but he was not.
我们被引导去相信史蒂夫在那扇门后面，但他并没有。

381
00:17:05.950 --> 00:17:08.210
He was probably prepping for a film.
他可能在为拍电影做准备。

382
00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:11.610
Or maybe finally getting to sleep in for a second.
或者可能终于能稍微睡个懒觉了。

383
00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:12.250
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

384
00:17:12.390 --> 00:17:13.450
Having the morning off.
早上放假。

385
00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.850
I hope he had the morning off.
我希望他早上能放假。

386
00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:21.190
Dwight's cell phone rings and somehow Jim answers it on his little Bluetooth thing and
德怀特的手机响了，不知怎么的，吉姆用他那个小蓝牙设备接听了

387
00:17:21.190 --> 00:17:22.070
his, you know, his ear.
他的，你知道的，他的耳朵上。

388
00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:23.790
Do you remember those?
你还记得那些吗？

389
00:17:24.090 --> 00:17:24.530
Yes.
记得。

390
00:17:24.650 --> 00:17:26.150
And people would walk around with them.
而且人们会带着它们到处走。

391
00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:26.830
Yeah.
对。

392
00:17:27.070 --> 00:17:30.530
I mean, we kind of still have this like earbud thing that we do.
我是说，我们现在其实也还在用这种类似耳机的东西。

393
00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:34.130
But back in the day, y'all, those things were giant.
但在当年，各位，那玩意儿可巨大了。

394
00:17:34.310 --> 00:17:36.350
Did you see how big that thing was on Jim's ear?
你看到吉姆耳朵上那个东西有多大了吧？

395
00:17:36.550 --> 00:17:38.850
This is an old tech alert for sure.
这绝对是个旧科技警报。

396
00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.530
And it is starting to drive Dwight crazy.
而且它开始把德怀特逼疯了。

397
00:17:41.770 --> 00:17:43.930
Why are all of his calls going to Jim?
为什么他的所有电话都转到吉姆那儿去了？

398
00:17:44.090 --> 00:17:47.730
Jim explains that Dwight left his cell phone on his desk.
吉姆解释说德怀特把手机忘在他桌上了。

399
00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:52.130
So naturally, he paired it to his headset, but it goes on.
所以很自然地，他把它配对到了自己的耳机上，但还没完。

400
00:17:52.530 --> 00:17:56.390
Dwight's like, fine, then I'm going to reprogram my cell phone to go to my desk.
德怀特就说，好吧，那我要把我的手机重新编程，转到我的桌子上。

401
00:17:56.710 --> 00:17:58.630
Well, Jim took care of that too.
好吧，吉姆也把那件事处理了。

402
00:17:58.810 --> 00:18:01.130
He forwarded Dwight's desk phone to his desk phone.
他把德怀特的座机呼叫转移到了自己的座机上。

403
00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:07.830
You know, I'm probably going to get some hate for this, but it does make me feel like Ryan
你知道的，我这么说可能会招黑，但这也让我觉得莱恩

404
00:18:07.830 --> 00:18:13.710
was correct in sort of calling Jim out on his productivity because look at all the effort
某种程度上质疑吉姆的工作效率是有道理的，因为你看他

405
00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:16.570
he went into this whole like earpiece prank.
为了整个耳机恶作剧花了多少精力。

406
00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.390
And he probably could have made some sales during this time.
而且他本来可以在这段时间里签下几单业务的。

407
00:18:19.570 --> 00:18:24.090
Here's what I want to say about that, because I worked in corporate America for a long time
对于这一点我想说的是，因为我在美国企业界工作了很长时间

408
00:18:24.090 --> 00:18:30.290
and I often felt like I could get all of my work done in about five hours, but I was required
我经常觉得自己大概五个小时就能干完所有的活，但公司硬性要求

409
00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.590
to sit there for eight.
我必须在那里坐满八个小时。

410
00:18:31.950 --> 00:18:32.130
Yeah.
没错。

411
00:18:32.310 --> 00:18:38.570
I mean, sometimes you can get what needs to be done faster than the company has allotted.
我的意思是，有时候你完成工作的时间确实比公司预留的要快。

412
00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:41.230
And so I think that was the case with Jim.
所以我觉得吉姆就是这种情况。

413
00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:43.130
I think he does very good in sales.
我觉得他的销售业绩非常棒。

414
00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:43.970
I don't know.
我不知道。

415
00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:47.930
I guess Ryan was like, what if you really spent those extra hours making sales?
我猜莱恩的意思是，要是你把那些多出来的时间真的用来做销售会怎么样？

416
00:18:48.110 --> 00:18:49.110
But I don't know.
不过我不知道。

417
00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:50.190
He's getting it done.
他反正把工作完成了。

418
00:18:50.410 --> 00:18:55.850
And he's I mean, sometimes I feel like these work hours are rather arbitrary.
而且我的意思是，有时候我觉得这些工作时间其实挺随意的。

419
00:18:56.110 --> 00:18:59.410
How about work until your work is done and then go home and enjoy your life?
干脆改成工作干完了就回家享受生活怎么样？

420
00:18:59.410 --> 00:19:00.630
I like that.
我喜欢这个主意。

421
00:19:00.930 --> 00:19:04.750
Jenna, you sound like some upstart company where you're like, here's the thing.
珍娜，你听起来就像那种新兴创业公司，会说：情况是这样的。

422
00:19:04.890 --> 00:19:06.110
Everyone gets pockets.
每个人都有口袋。

423
00:19:06.410 --> 00:19:06.750
Yes.
对。

424
00:19:06.990 --> 00:19:08.910
You work as long as you want.
你想工作多久就工作多久。

425
00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:09.930
Get your done.
把你的活干完就行。

426
00:19:10.190 --> 00:19:10.930
We don't care.
我们不在乎。

427
00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:16.730
Also, we have a soapbox in the lobby and you can stand on it at any point in your day if
另外，我们在大厅里设了一个肥皂箱演讲台，你可以在一天中的任何时候站上去

428
00:19:16.730 --> 00:19:19.010
you need to make any declarations about anything.
如果你需要对任何事情发表宣言的话。

429
00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:19.650
Yeah.
对。

430
00:19:19.790 --> 00:19:24.650
And finally, we have like a zombie apocalypse shelter ready to go.
最后，我们还准备好了一个僵尸末日避难所。

431
00:19:24.790 --> 00:19:24.970
Yeah.
对。

432
00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.030
We have a panic room totally stocked.
我们有一个物资备齐的安全屋。

433
00:19:27.210 --> 00:19:28.190
That's Jenna's company.
那就是珍娜的公司。

434
00:19:28.190 --> 00:19:29.490
Who wants to work for me?
谁想给我打工？

435
00:19:29.730 --> 00:19:30.710
Come work for me.
快来给我打工吧。

436
00:19:30.870 --> 00:19:31.770
That sounds amazing.
听起来太棒了。

437
00:19:32.110 --> 00:19:33.310
You know what is funny?
你知道什么好笑吗？

438
00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:36.490
I've basically created that job with this podcaSt.
我基本上通过这个播客创造了那样的工作岗位。

439
00:19:36.870 --> 00:19:37.510
You have.
你确实有。

440
00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:41.210
You've given yourself all of those things, except maybe the zombie apocalypse room.
你给自己配齐了所有这些东西，除了可能没有僵尸末日安全屋。

441
00:19:41.390 --> 00:19:41.750
I don't know.
我不知道。

442
00:19:41.870 --> 00:19:42.470
Do you have a wait?
等等，你有吗？

443
00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:43.610
Is there something you need to tell me?
有什么事需要跟我坦白吗？

444
00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:46.830
I don't have a whole room, but I've got all my backpacks ready to go.
我虽然没有一整间屋子，但我的双肩包都已经随时准备出发了。

445
00:19:48.850 --> 00:19:51.390
I have a catch for this cold open.
我对这段片头有个发现。

446
00:19:51.690 --> 00:19:52.670
It's a Jenna catch.
这是一个珍娜式的发现。

447
00:19:53.190 --> 00:19:56.610
During this cold open, Jim pretends to talk to Dwight's mother.
在这段片头里，吉姆假装在跟德怀特的母亲通话。

448
00:19:56.950 --> 00:19:57.170
Yeah.
对。

449
00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:57.570
Right?
是吧？

450
00:19:57.770 --> 00:20:00.690
He says, mother, tell father I'm getting married.
他说，母亲，告诉父亲我要结婚了。

451
00:20:01.150 --> 00:20:01.590
Yeah.
是啊。

452
00:20:01.950 --> 00:20:07.470
Well, in Fun Run, do you remember, Angela, when Dwight is trying to make your character feel
话说在“趣味跑”那一集里，安吉拉，你还记得当德怀特试图让你的角色

453
00:20:07.470 --> 00:20:09.190
better about sprinkles dying?
对“洒水车”的死感觉好一点时吗？

454
00:20:09.450 --> 00:20:16.490
He offers to have sprinkles stuffed or he offers to have sprinkles buried in the East
他提出要把“洒水车”做成标本，或者提议把它埋在妈妈的

455
00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:18.170
Field by mother.
东边田地里。

456
00:20:18.750 --> 00:20:18.890
Yeah.
对。

457
00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:20.690
Dwight's mother is not living.
德怀特的妈妈已经不在了。

458
00:20:21.170 --> 00:20:21.430
Yeah.
是啊。

459
00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:23.850
Ah, little continuity error.
啊，一个小小的剧情漏洞。

460
00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:26.450
Yes, I was very proud of my catch.
是的，我为自己能挑出这个毛病感到很自豪。

461
00:20:26.970 --> 00:20:28.470
Well done, Jenna.
干得好，珍娜。

462
00:20:29.170 --> 00:20:30.030
Guess what?
你猜怎么着？

463
00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:30.590
What?
什么？

464
00:20:30.910 --> 00:20:32.410
It's Toby's last day.
今天是托比的最后一天。

465
00:20:32.890 --> 00:20:34.690
Michael is dancing through the office.
迈克尔在办公室里手舞足蹈。

466
00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.170
He's gotten there so early.
他到得太早了。

467
00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:38.430
No one is there and he's literally dancing.
根本没人来，而他真的在跳舞。

468
00:20:38.750 --> 00:20:43.390
I mean, he says today is one of those days you know you will remember for the rest of your
我的意思是，他说今天是那种你知道自己余生都会铭记的

469
00:20:43.390 --> 00:20:43.850
life.
日子。

470
00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:44.530
I know.
我知道。

471
00:20:44.790 --> 00:20:48.710
It's a countdown until his horribleness is out of the building.
这是在倒计时，直到这个讨厌鬼滚出这栋大楼。

472
00:20:49.210 --> 00:20:56.110
He sets an alarm on his watch that's going to go off as Toby has his final moments in
他在手表上设置了一个闹钟，正好会在托比在办公室的

473
00:20:56.110 --> 00:20:56.610
the office.
最后时刻响起。

474
00:20:56.770 --> 00:20:57.670
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

475
00:20:57.850 --> 00:20:58.390
He's giddy.
他乐开了花。

476
00:20:58.710 --> 00:20:59.710
Toby arrives.
托比到了。

477
00:20:59.970 --> 00:21:03.450
He goes back to HR and Kelly hugs him.
他回到人事部，凯莉拥抱了他。

478
00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:04.930
She can't believe it's his last day.
她简直不敢相信这是他的最后一天。

479
00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:06.010
She feels so weird.
她觉得太不可思议了。

480
00:21:06.250 --> 00:21:07.590
Toby feels fine.
托比感觉挺好的。

481
00:21:07.770 --> 00:21:08.810
He's not upset.
他并没有难过。

482
00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:09.490
Yeah.
是啊。

483
00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:10.570
All right.
好吧。

484
00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.290
Conference room meeting, Angela.
会议室开会了，安吉拉。

485
00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:16.370
The party planning committee is going to discuss Toby's goodbye party.
派对策划委员会要讨论托比的欢送派对。

486
00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:18.650
I loved every minute of this scene.
我喜欢这场戏的每一分钟。

487
00:21:18.810 --> 00:21:20.590
I loved every minute of doing it.
我喜欢拍摄它的每一分钟。

488
00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.170
I loved every minute of watching it.
我喜欢看它的每一分钟。

489
00:21:22.590 --> 00:21:24.650
I am so very pregnant.
我当时怀孕非常明显。

490
00:21:25.050 --> 00:21:27.950
I am at that stage in pregnancy where you can't hide it.
我已经到了怀孕那种藏都藏不住的阶段。

491
00:21:28.010 --> 00:21:28.790
Look at my face.
看我的脸。

492
00:21:29.190 --> 00:21:31.510
No, your belly is practically in your neck.
不，你的肚子几乎快贴到脖子上了。

493
00:21:31.650 --> 00:21:32.690
Let's be honeSt.
说实话。

494
00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:34.650
I don't know how you fit under that table.
我不知道你是怎么塞进那张桌子底下的。

495
00:21:34.990 --> 00:21:37.050
I'm a short person, you guys.
各位，我是个矮个子。

496
00:21:37.050 --> 00:21:39.550
Tall people, when they're pregnant, they go up.
高个子怀孕时，肚子是往上长的。

497
00:21:39.750 --> 00:21:42.370
But when you're short, you just go out.
但如果你个子矮，就只能往前长。

498
00:21:42.570 --> 00:21:45.890
And it was like my head was sitting on top of my belly.
而且感觉我的头就像直接顶在肚子上一样。

499
00:21:46.310 --> 00:21:49.430
Angela tells Michael, here's what they've got for the party.
安吉拉告诉迈克尔，这是他们为派对准备的东西。

500
00:21:49.610 --> 00:21:54.790
A buttercream cake and a slideshow of Toby, but they only have two photos of Toby.
一个奶油蛋糕和一段托比的幻灯片，但他们只有两张托比的照片。

501
00:21:55.350 --> 00:21:59.470
They're just two different expressions standing getting coffee in the kitchen.
他们只是在厨房里买咖啡时表现出两种不同的表情。

502
00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:00.290
It's amazing.
这太神奇了。

503
00:22:00.690 --> 00:22:02.950
Michael is like, absolutely not.
迈克尔的态度是，绝对不行。

504
00:22:03.130 --> 00:22:03.590
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

505
00:22:03.730 --> 00:22:05.270
This needs to be very special.
这必须非常特别。

506
00:22:05.270 --> 00:22:07.850
Toby is going away forever.
托比就要永远离开了。

507
00:22:08.190 --> 00:22:11.130
He wants the party to end all parties.
他想要办一场空前绝后的派对。

508
00:22:11.630 --> 00:22:11.810
Yeah.
是啊。

509
00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:16.590
He says when someone in New Orleans leaves, they throw a parade for them.
他说在新奥尔良有人离开时，会为他们举办一场游行。

510
00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:21.170
And Pam says, you want to throw Toby a New Orleans funeral?
然后潘说，你是想给托比办一场新奥尔良葬礼吗？

511
00:22:21.430 --> 00:22:23.030
Because that's what that means.
因为那就是那个意思。

512
00:22:23.170 --> 00:22:25.090
That's the parade Michael is talking about.
那就是迈克尔所说的游行。

513
00:22:25.290 --> 00:22:30.470
In the shooting draft, Jenna, there were a few more extra lines to the scene that really tickled me.
珍娜，在拍摄剧本中，这场戏还有一些额外的台词让我觉得很好笑。

514
00:22:30.470 --> 00:22:32.390
So Pam says that line.
所以潘说了那句台词。

515
00:22:32.550 --> 00:22:35.310
And then Michael says, if that's appropriate, then that's what I want.
然后迈克尔说，如果那很合适，那这就是我想要的。

516
00:22:35.450 --> 00:22:37.630
I want something that says, oh, wow.
我想要那种能让人感叹，哦，哇。

517
00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:38.510
Okay.
好吧。

518
00:22:38.810 --> 00:22:39.650
Oh, God.
哦，天哪。

519
00:22:39.890 --> 00:22:41.050
Thank God.
谢天谢地。

520
00:22:41.710 --> 00:22:44.610
And then Angela says, a prayer?
然后安吉拉说，一个祈祷？

521
00:22:44.810 --> 00:22:46.490
You want a prayer party?
你想要一个祈祷派对？

522
00:22:46.970 --> 00:22:53.410
And then that's when Michael says, if the devil were to explode and evil disappeared, that's what he says in the script.
然后就在那时迈克尔说，如果魔鬼爆炸了，邪恶消失了，他在剧本里是这么说的。

523
00:22:53.410 --> 00:22:55.490
That's the kind of party I want to throw.
那就是我想办的派对。

524
00:22:55.870 --> 00:23:01.850
Angela explains they only have enough money for a cake and maybe to develop a few more slides.
安吉拉解释说，他们的钱只够买一个蛋糕，或许还能冲洗一些幻灯片。

525
00:23:02.130 --> 00:23:03.410
Toby will not be in them.
托比不会出现在幻灯片里。

526
00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:06.530
And that is when Michael gets out his shoe.
然后就在那时，迈克尔拿出了他的鞋子。

527
00:23:06.710 --> 00:23:07.510
As one does.
理所当然。

528
00:23:07.510 --> 00:23:12.350
You get out your shoe, you pull up the insole, and you have a wad of cash.
你脱下鞋子，掀开鞋垫，里面有一卷现金。

529
00:23:13.010 --> 00:23:13.230
Yeah.
是啊。

530
00:23:13.550 --> 00:23:17.350
Michael explains every year his grandma sends him $50 for his birthday.
迈克尔解释说，他奶奶每年生日都会给他寄50美元。

531
00:23:17.350 --> 00:23:21.170
But lately, she's been sending him about nine or 10 checks a year.
但最近，她一年大概会给他寄九到十张支票。

532
00:23:21.430 --> 00:23:23.990
He was saving for a motorcycle, Angela.
安吉拉，他本来是在存钱买摩托车的。

533
00:23:24.230 --> 00:23:26.790
But he thinks this is what he wants to spend his money on.
但他觉得这是他现在想把钱花在上面的地方。

534
00:23:27.150 --> 00:23:29.430
We had a fan question from Isabella D.
我们收到了来自伊莎贝拉·D的粉丝提问。

535
00:23:29.810 --> 00:23:36.450
In Catcher in the Rye, Holden says that his loaded grandmother has been losing her marbles a little bit
在《麦田里的守望者》中，霍尔顿说他富有而祖母有点神志不清了，

536
00:23:36.450 --> 00:23:40.290
and has been sending him money for his birthday multiple times a year.
一年中多次给他寄生日钱。

537
00:23:40.610 --> 00:23:44.110
Was this a happy coincidence or an intentional reference?
这是一个巧合还是有意为之的梗？

538
00:23:44.330 --> 00:23:45.830
And who came up with it?
是谁想出来的？

539
00:23:46.170 --> 00:23:47.010
I don't know.
我不知道。

540
00:23:47.350 --> 00:23:48.250
Do you know?
你知道吗？

541
00:23:48.550 --> 00:23:49.490
I found out.
我查到了。

542
00:23:49.730 --> 00:23:50.930
Paul wrote this.
保罗写的这个。

543
00:23:50.930 --> 00:23:53.170
He said it was not intentional.
他说这不是故意的。

544
00:23:53.230 --> 00:23:54.950
It's just a happy coincidence.
这只是一个巧合。

545
00:23:54.950 --> 00:23:57.630
But I would like to say, Isabella D.
但我想说，伊莎贝拉·D。

546
00:23:58.130 --> 00:23:58.730
Applause.
掌声。

547
00:23:59.370 --> 00:24:02.210
I applaud you for being very, very well read.
我为你博览群书而鼓掌。

548
00:24:02.430 --> 00:24:02.910
Yes.
是的。

549
00:24:03.090 --> 00:24:05.970
And bringing up this literary parallel reference.
并提出了这个文学平行对照的梗。

550
00:24:06.610 --> 00:24:07.050
Yeah.
是啊。

551
00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:11.770
Well, Michael starts listing all of these ridiculous things he wants at this party.
迈克尔开始列出他在派对上想要的各种荒唐的东西。

552
00:24:11.950 --> 00:24:17.090
He says he wants to feel like he's flying through the air without this ugly weight holding
他说他想感觉自己像是在空中飞翔，没有这个丑陋的累赘

553
00:24:17.090 --> 00:24:17.610
him down.
拖着他。

554
00:24:17.790 --> 00:24:19.670
He wants an anti-gravity machine.
他想要一台反重力机器。

555
00:24:19.850 --> 00:24:20.710
And you know what?
你知道吗？

556
00:24:21.050 --> 00:24:22.030
Angela has had it.
安吉拉忍无可忍了。

557
00:24:22.170 --> 00:24:23.010
She has had it.
她是真的忍够了。

558
00:24:23.070 --> 00:24:24.730
She said she doesn't want his foot money.
她说她不要他那沾脚的脏钱。

559
00:24:24.950 --> 00:24:26.530
Oh, that made me laugh out loud, lady.
哦，天哪，女士，这把我逗得哈哈大笑。

560
00:24:26.850 --> 00:24:28.150
I loved foot money.
我很喜欢那笔“脚气钱”。

561
00:24:28.370 --> 00:24:29.930
I mean, I laughed out loud.
我是说，我真的笑出声了。

562
00:24:30.450 --> 00:24:34.790
You know, in the script, Jenna, I looked because I was curious about the direction of the scene.
珍娜，你知道的，我查了剧本，因为我对这场戏的场记很好奇。

563
00:24:35.010 --> 00:24:38.430
And it says that Angela pushes the money back towards Michael.
上面写着安吉拉把钱推回给迈克尔。

564
00:24:38.770 --> 00:24:41.610
And I added that I did it with my pen.
我加了点戏，我是用笔推回去的。

565
00:24:41.790 --> 00:24:42.470
That was me.
那是我的即兴发挥。

566
00:24:42.470 --> 00:24:43.890
That's what I loved about it.
这就是我最喜欢它的地方。

567
00:24:44.030 --> 00:24:45.410
You didn't even want to touch it.
你甚至都不想碰它。

568
00:24:45.650 --> 00:24:45.870
No.
对。

569
00:24:45.990 --> 00:24:47.610
It disgusted you so much.
它让你感到太恶心了。

570
00:24:47.910 --> 00:24:48.170
Yeah.
是的。

571
00:24:48.190 --> 00:24:49.590
But it was so fun.
但真的很有趣。

572
00:24:49.750 --> 00:24:52.230
I remember us getting really tickled, Jenna.
我记得我们当时笑得前仰后合，珍娜。

573
00:24:52.610 --> 00:24:53.190
Oh, my gosh.
哦，天哪。

574
00:24:53.270 --> 00:24:56.510
We loved these scenes with Steve and the party planning committee.
我们超爱和史蒂夫以及派对策划委员会拍这些对手戏。

575
00:24:56.670 --> 00:24:58.750
They are truly some of my favorite to shoot.
它们绝对是我最喜欢拍摄的场景之一。

576
00:24:59.110 --> 00:24:59.330
Yeah.
没错。

577
00:24:59.410 --> 00:25:00.170
It was just candy.
这简直就是一种享受。

578
00:25:00.310 --> 00:25:01.190
It didn't feel like work.
感觉根本不像在工作。

579
00:25:01.190 --> 00:25:02.350
I just couldn't wait.
我简直迫不及待。

580
00:25:02.390 --> 00:25:06.410
And my biggest goal was just to not laugh so that we could get some usable footage.
我最大的目标就是别笑场，好让我们能拍出点能用的素材。

581
00:25:06.730 --> 00:25:10.010
Well, now Michael is going to put Phyllis in charge.
好了，现在迈克尔要让菲莉丝来负责了。

582
00:25:10.010 --> 00:25:12.830
Oh, I loved it so much.
哦，我太喜欢这个了。

583
00:25:13.050 --> 00:25:14.590
Phyllis crushed it.
菲莉丝演得太棒了。

584
00:25:14.810 --> 00:25:20.010
The way she said yes, when Michael asked her if she will plan the party,
当迈克尔问她愿不愿意策划派对时，她答应的那种语气，

585
00:25:20.250 --> 00:25:24.190
it is like she has waited for this moment her whole life.
就像她一辈子都在等待这一刻一样。

586
00:25:24.570 --> 00:25:27.050
So I have a little script tidbit to share.
所以我有一个小小的剧本花絮要分享。

587
00:25:27.290 --> 00:25:32.910
After Phyllis says yes, it would have cut immediately to an Angela talking head.
在菲莉丝答应之后，镜头本该立刻切到一个安吉拉的访谈镜头。

588
00:25:33.050 --> 00:25:37.690
And it says Angela's talking head just starts with a huge fake laugh.
上面写着安吉拉的访谈一开始就是一声巨大的假笑。

589
00:25:37.690 --> 00:25:45.950
And then Angela says, I was going to let Phyllis be in charge of cups today.
然后安吉拉说，我本打算让菲莉丝今天负责杯子的。

590
00:25:46.150 --> 00:25:51.030
And even then, I had a stack of cups standing by in my trunk.
即便如此，我后备箱里还备着一叠杯子呢。

591
00:25:51.990 --> 00:25:53.390
Of course you did.
你当然会这样。

592
00:25:54.410 --> 00:25:55.750
Isn't that so good?
是不是很棒？

593
00:25:56.090 --> 00:25:59.990
They must have just loved writing those snarky talking heads for you, Angela.
他们肯定特别喜欢为你写那些刻薄的单人访谈，安吉拉。

594
00:26:00.110 --> 00:26:00.810
They're so good.
真的太精彩了。

595
00:26:01.110 --> 00:26:03.130
I was going to let her be in charge of cups.
我本打算让她负责杯子的。

596
00:26:03.310 --> 00:26:03.750
Sort of.
算是吧。

597
00:26:03.890 --> 00:26:05.210
But I doubt she could handle it.
但我怀疑她应付得来。

598
00:26:05.490 --> 00:26:06.730
Well, now the big moment.
好吧，现在是高光时刻了。

599
00:26:08.030 --> 00:26:10.010
Holly Flax arrives.
霍莉·弗拉克斯来了。

600
00:26:10.430 --> 00:26:11.530
New HR rep.
新来的HR代表。

601
00:26:12.390 --> 00:26:12.750
Yes.
是的。

602
00:26:13.110 --> 00:26:16.350
And Toby has a talking head that as part of his last day,
托比有一个单人访谈镜头，作为他最后一天的一部分，

603
00:26:16.510 --> 00:26:19.790
he's going to be training the new human resources rep.
他将培训新的行政人事代表。

604
00:26:19.970 --> 00:26:24.310
And he says, again, the company has allotted only one day for this.
他说，再次强调，公司只为这事分配了一天时间。

605
00:26:24.590 --> 00:26:25.690
One training day.
培训只有一天。

606
00:26:25.810 --> 00:26:26.470
That's all you need.
这就够了。

607
00:26:26.810 --> 00:26:27.610
That's it?
这就没了？

608
00:26:27.990 --> 00:26:28.370
Yeah.
是的。

609
00:26:28.870 --> 00:26:32.230
That's all you're going to say about this moment in the show.
这就是你对节目里这个时刻要说全部的话吗。

610
00:26:32.450 --> 00:26:32.890
What?
什么？

611
00:26:32.890 --> 00:26:34.890
What are you hinting at?
你在暗示什么？

612
00:26:35.270 --> 00:26:37.410
I can't believe I have to bring this up.
真不敢相信我得提起这个。

613
00:26:37.890 --> 00:26:38.370
Lady.
女士。

614
00:26:38.670 --> 00:26:38.970
What?
什么？

615
00:26:39.150 --> 00:26:41.690
The blooming plant at reception?
前台那盆开花的植物？

616
00:26:42.310 --> 00:26:43.110
Hold up.
等等。

617
00:26:43.490 --> 00:26:45.150
With your shade, Jenna Fisher.
真有你的，珍娜·费舍。

618
00:26:45.790 --> 00:26:48.930
I have a whole plant breakdown I was going to bring up later.
我本来准备了一整套关于植物的分析打算一会儿说呢。

619
00:26:49.130 --> 00:26:49.770
Thank you very much.
非常感谢。

620
00:26:49.770 --> 00:26:51.790
I was going to let Holly have her moment.
我本想让霍莉享受她的高光时刻。

621
00:26:52.490 --> 00:26:52.850
Oh.
哦。

622
00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:53.810
All right.
好吧。

623
00:26:53.950 --> 00:26:55.250
Well, I shouldn't have doubted you.
行吧，我不该怀疑你的。

624
00:26:55.390 --> 00:26:55.810
I'm sorry.
对不起。

625
00:26:55.990 --> 00:26:56.610
Don't doubt me.
别怀疑我。

626
00:26:56.730 --> 00:26:59.810
But I mean, all I saw was a blooming plant at reception.
但我的意思是，我看到的只有前台那盆开花的植物。

627
00:26:59.830 --> 00:27:02.250
She's carrying a plant in her box.
她抱着一个箱子，里面有株植物。

628
00:27:02.250 --> 00:27:04.150
It was just like a plant explosion.
简直就像是一场植物大爆炸。

629
00:27:04.470 --> 00:27:08.750
And as I was watching this episode, I thought, well, Angela is just going to love that.
当我看着这一集的时候，我想，安吉拉肯定会超喜欢那个。

630
